### Expense Tracker -- demo.http
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or IntelliJ's built-in
### HTTP Client. Run `make up` first -- every request below hits the real,
### locally-running stack (authorization-server :9000, resource-server :8082,
### bff-client :8080). Covers SPEC.md's endpoint -> authorization-style map.
###
### The interactive login (username/password + consent) can't be scripted as
### a plain HTTP request -- it's a multi-step browser dance. Either open
### http://localhost:8080/ in a browser and log in as one of the seeded users
### below, or run the automated version:
### `mvn -q -pl integration-tests -am verify` (see CodeGrantEndToEndIT).
###
### Seeded users: alice/alice-demo-pw (acme, EMPLOYEE), bob/bob-demo-pw (acme,
### MANAGER), carol/carol-demo-pw (globex, FINANCE), dana/dana-demo-pw
### (globex, ORG_ADMIN).

@authServer = http://localhost:9000
@resourceServer = http://localhost:8082
@bffClient = http://localhost:8080

### [style: public] Categories -- no token needed.
GET {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/categories

### --- M2M: client_credentials, no browser, no cookies ------------------

### Get a token for export-worker (scope: expenses.export).
# @name clientCredentialsToken
POST {{authServer}}/oauth2/token
Authorization: Basic ZXhwb3J0LXdvcmtlcjpleHBvcnQtd29ya2VyLXNlY3JldA==
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=expenses.export

### [style: scope-gated M2M] Export -- not org-scoped by design (an export
### job runs across every tenant). Paste the access_token from the response
### above into @m2mToken.
@m2mToken = paste-access-token-here

GET {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/reports/export
Authorization: Bearer {{m2mToken}}

### --- Everything below needs a real user's access token -----------------
### Log in at http://localhost:8080/ (any seeded user), open DevTools ->
### Application -> Cookies, and paste the SESSION cookie value below to call
### bff-client's own SPA-facing endpoints with the same session a real
### browser would use. Or, if you have a user access token from
### CodeGrantEndToEndIT / your own manual authorization_code run, use
### @userToken directly against resource-server instead.

@sessionCookie = paste-SESSION-cookie-value-here
@userToken = paste-user-access-token-here

### [style: authenticated, any role] whoami via the BFF (session cookie, no
### token visible to the browser at all -- this is the point of [FEATURE B1]).
GET {{bffClient}}/whoami
Cookie: SESSION={{sessionCookie}}

### [style: authenticated, any role] whoami directly against resource-server
### (bearer token -- what the BFF is doing on your behalf above).
GET {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### [style: collection filtering] List reports -- @PostFilter drops drafts
### that aren't the caller's own (log in as bob to see this: alice's DRAFT
### "Conference trip planning" never appears in bob's list).
GET {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### [style: owner-only] Get one of alice's own reports (log in as alice).
GET {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/reports/e2222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### [style: owner-only] Update it (log in as alice -- anyone else gets 403).
PUT {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/reports/e2222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "0"

{
  "title": "Q1 client travel (updated)",
  "description": "Site visits to two clients, revised itinerary",
  "currency": "USD"
}

### [style: role-gated] Approve a report -- ROLE_MANAGER only (log in as bob).
POST {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/reports/e3333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### [style: field redaction] Reimbursements -- IBAN masked unless
### ROLE_FINANCE (log in as carol to see the real IBAN; anyone else sees it
### masked).
GET {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/reimbursements
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### [style: meta-annotation, @IsOrgAdmin] Delete a report -- ORG_ADMIN only
### (log in as dana; alice's DRAFT below is in a *different* org, so this
### also proves tenant scoping -- expect 403, not 404).
DELETE {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/reports/e1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### --- Negative paths (see integration-tests/.../CodeGrantEndToEndIT for
### the automated, assertion-backed versions of these) --------------------

### Cross-org access -> 403 with an RFC 9457 body (dana is globex, this
### report is acme's).
GET {{resourceServer}}/api/v1/reports/e2222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Absent CSRF token on a state-changing bff-client request -> 403.
POST {{bffClient}}/api/reports
Cookie: SESSION={{sessionCookie}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Should be rejected -- no X-XSRF-TOKEN header"}
